    "body": "So basically I think it probably means that can be removed from the compat spec. The only thing is that browsers can't possibly get rid of the `-webkit-` values, because many sites rely on them. \r\n\r\nAs of today \r\n\r\n* [`background-clip`: 36% usage](https://chromestatus.com/metrics/css/popularity#background-clip)\r\n* [`-webkit-background-clip`:  8%](https://chromestatus.com/metrics/css/popularity#webkit-background-clip) ❗and climbing. \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
