    "updated_at": "2022-06-16T14:29:42Z",
    "body": "> Or is there a specific section needed about all the prefixed properties, we can't remove even if well implemented because the Web relies on them? :)\r\n\r\nYep! That's kind of the whole point for the spec. If a different spec wants to spec the prefixed variant, we can remove them then: an example, https://www.w3.org/TR/geometry-1/#webkitcssmatrix, which \"started\" here). But we want them to be defined _somewhere_.",
